            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^2(3x^2-1)\\,dx$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$6$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^2(3x^2-1)\\,dx&=[x^3-x]_0^2\\\\&=(8-2)-0\\\\&=6\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 24
          },
          {
            "id": "p20-q7-b",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "b",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_2^0(3x^2-1)\\,dx$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$-6$. The values in a and b are opposites because the limits are reversed.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_2^0(3x^2-1)\\,dx&=[x^3-x]_2^0\\\\&=0-(8-2)\\\\&=-6\\end{aligned}$$\nThe integrals in a and b are opposites because the limits have been reversed.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 31
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7-cd",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 2,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [
          {
            "id": "p20-q7-c",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "c",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle\\int_0^1 20x^3\\,dx$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$5$",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^1 20x^3\\,dx&=[5x^4]_0^1\\\\&=5\\end{aligned}$$",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 21
          },
          {
            "id": "p20-q7-d",
            "type": "part",
            "label": "d",
            "prompt": "$\\displaystyle20\\int_0^1 x^3\\,dx$",
            "layout": "list",
            "columns": null,
            "questionDiagrams": [],
            "children": [],
            "answer": {
              "short": "$5$. A constant factor can be taken out of the integral, so c and d are equal.",
              "worked": "$$\\begin{aligned}20\\int_0^1 x^3\\,dx&=20\\left[\\frac{x^4}{4}\\right]_0^1\\\\&=20\\left(\\frac14\\right)\\\\&=5\\end{aligned}$$\nA constant factor can be taken out of the integral, so c and d are equal.",
              "solutionDiagrams": []
            },
            "answerSpaceMm": 33
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "id": "p20-q7-eg",
        "type": "group",
        "label": "",
        "prompt": "",
        "layout": "grid",
        "columns": 3,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
